# .public-genericize.example — template for params/.public-genericize
#
# Copy to params/.public-genericize (that folder is gitignored, so the file — and
# the real identifiers in it — are never committed or synced to the public mirror).
#
# scripts/sync-to-public.sh applies this map to the sanitized EXPORT tree BEFORE the
# fail-closed content deny-scan: one `ERE_pattern|replacement` per line ('#' =
# comment). Each real value is rewritten to a generic placeholder so base manifests,
# Helm valueFiles, instance data (game servers, NAS shares), scripts, docs and
# platform.yaml stay publishable as a forkable TEMPLATE — instead of being stripped
# or hardcoding your real domain/IPs into the public mirror.
#
# It is applied to the export COPY only, never to the private source ArgoCD deploys,
# so it can never affect prod. ENVSUBST-rendered manifests already carry
# ${BASE_DOMAIN}-style tokens, so these subs are a no-op there.
#
# Pair this 1:1 with params/.public-deny: for every private identifier you DENY,
# give its public placeholder here. If a deny pattern has no placeholder, the
# deny-scan will just abort the sync when that value appears (fail-closed) — safe,
# but the mirror never updates until you add the placeholder.
#
# Rules:
#   - ERE syntax (grep -E / sed -E). GNU \b word-boundaries are supported.
#   - The FIRST '|' splits pattern from replacement; do NOT use '|' inside either.
#   - Replacements may use sed backrefs (\1 \2) to preserve capture groups.
#
# IMPORTANT: CI publishes via .github/workflows/sync-to-public.yml, which
# materializes this map from the `PUBLIC_GENERICIZE_MAP` repo secret — NOT from this
# file. Keep the secret and this file in sync, or CI's transform will differ from a
# local `sync-to-public.sh` run.
#
your-real-domain\.com|example.com
your-github-owner|example-owner
# Real usernames / handles (word-boundaried to avoid over-matching):
# \byourhandle\b|admin
# Real RFC1918 ranges (preserve host octets via backrefs; map to a documentation range):
# \b10\.10\.([0-9]+)\.([0-9]+)\b|10.0.\1.\2
# \b10\.25\.([0-9]+)\.([0-9]+)\b|10.1.\1.\2
# Real storage/export paths:
# /mnt/YourPool/|/mnt/pool/
